t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Constructs a new <code>stop_source</code> object.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Constructs a <code>stop_source</code> with new stop-state.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Constructs an empty <code>stop_source</code> with no associated stop-state.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3)</span> Copy constructor. Constructs a <code>stop_source</code> whose associated stop-state is the same as that of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> Move constructor. Constructs a <code>stop_source</code> whose associated stop-state is the same as that of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>; <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> is left empty.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> nss\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> an <code>std::nostopstate_t</code> placeholder object to construct an empty <code>stop_source</code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> other\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> another <code>stop_source</code> object to construct this <code>stop_source</code> object with\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Postconditions\">Postconditions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> <span class=\"t-lc\">stop_possible()</span> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> and <span class=\"t-lc\">stop_requested()</span> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>. </div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> <span class=\"t-lc\">stop_possible()</span> and <span class=\"t-lc\">stop_requested()</span> are both <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> share the same associated stop-state and compare equal.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> has <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>'s previously associated stop-state, and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">stop_possible</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\">std::bad_alloc</a></span> if memory could not be allocated for the stop-state.</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Postconditions","id":"Postconditions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"thread","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"thread/stop_source","title":"std::stop_source"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::stop_source::stop_source","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Constructs a new stop_source object."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"nss, other"},{"label":"Postconditions","note":"stop_possible() is true and stop_requested() is false."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"std::bad_alloc if memory could not be allo